{
  "assessment": "The source provides two quantitative regimes for ac conductivity in the SSH chain with chiral disorder: off-critical (Eq. soffcrit) and critical (Eq. sigcrit). Both are supported by analytical arguments and numerical fits. The off-critical regime uses the control delta (staggering parameter) with a fitted exponent 2|delta|, and the critical regime uses disorder strength s with a fitted log^2 amplitude. The source reports numerical fits for delta values 0.78, 0.78, 1.23, 1.24 and for critical case with s^2=0.3, c_crit=0.13. The extraction captures the central quantitative relations, parameters, and fixed conditions. The case is authoring-ready with two regimes sharing controls delta and s, and readouts sigma_offcrit and sigma_crit.",
  "case_authoring_ready": true,
  "source": {
    "citation": "Ilia Komissarov, Quantum Critical Dynamics Induced by Topological Zero Modes, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/z8v9-f8j2",
    "journal_doi": "10.1103/z8v9-f8j2",
    "arxiv_versioned_id": "2502.12233v2"
  },
  "paper_scope": "The paper studies low-frequency ac transport in the Su-Schrieffer-Heeger (SSH) chain with chiral disorder, focusing on the topological delocalization transition. It derives scaling laws for ac conductivity at criticality (logarithmic) and away from criticality (power-law with log^2 corrections), using real-space renormalization group and Mott hybridization arguments. The selected quantitative cluster covers the off-critical and critical ac conductivity formulas, their parameters, and numerical verification.",
  "mechanisms": [
    {
      "mechanism_id": "mott_hybridization_offcrit",
      "statement": "Away from criticality, zero modes hybridize into bonding/anti-bonding pairs with energy splitting exponentially small in segment length; the dipole matrix element scales as d ~ xi0 log omega, and the density of states is algebraic, leading to ac conductivity sigma ~ omega^{2|delta|} log^2 omega.",
      "equations": [
        "|braket{psi_+|x|psi_-}| ~ d ~ xi0 log omega",
        "nu_topo(E) ~ |E|^{-1+2|delta|}",
        "sigma(omega) ~ omega^{2|delta|} log^2 omega"
      ],
      "variable_names": ["delta", "omega", "sigma", "d", "xi0", "nu"],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "offcrit_power_exponent",
          "value": 2,
          "uncertainty": "source_unspecified",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "exponent multiplying |delta| in the power-law factor of sigma(omega)",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 165,
              "line_end": 165,
              "support": "Equation (soffcrit) states sigma(omega) ~ omega^{2|delta|} log^2 omega."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "offcrit_log_exponent",
          "value": 2,
          "uncertainty": "source_unspecified",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "exponent of the logarithmic factor in sigma(omega)",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 165,
              "line_end": 165,
              "support": "Equation (soffcrit) states sigma(omega) ~ omega^{2|delta|} log^2 omega."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 184,
          "line_end": 190,
          "support": "Hybridization energy omega = Omega e^{-d/xi}, dipole matrix element ~ d ~ xi0 log omega."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 193,
          "line_end": 196,
          "support": "Density of states nu_topo(E) ~ |E|^{-1+2|delta|}, with |delta| = (xi/2)|log(1-p)|."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 213,
          "line_end": 217,
          "support": "Kubo-Greenwood summation yields sigma(omega) ~ omega^{2|delta|} log^2 omega."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "mechanism_id": "mott_hybridization_crit",
      "statement": "At criticality, zero modes decay stretched-exponentially as psi ~ e^{-s sqrt{x}}, leading to dipole matrix element ~ c_crit s^{-2} log^2(Omega/omega) and Dyson singularity in density of states, giving ac conductivity sigma_crit ~ s^{-2} log(Omega/omega).",
      "equations": [
        "psi_0(x) ~ e^{-s sqrt{x}}",
        "|braket{psi_{omega/2}|x|psi_{-omega/2}}|_crit = c_crit s^{-2} log^2(Omega/omega)",
        "nu_crit(E) = s^2 [|E| log^3(Omega/|E|)]^{-1}",
        "sigma_crit(omega) ~ s^{-2} log(Omega/omega)"
      ],
      "variable_names": ["s", "omega", "sigma_crit", "c_crit", "Omega", "psi"],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "crit_amplitude_coefficient",
          "value": 0.13,
          "uncertainty": "source_unspecified",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "coefficient c_crit in the dipole matrix element fit",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 247,
              "line_end": 247,
              "support": "Caption of plot3: predicted relation c_s = c_crit s^{-2} established with c_crit ~ 0.13."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "crit_log_exponent",
          "value": 2,
          "uncertainty": "source_unspecified",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "exponent of log in the dipole matrix element",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 257,
              "line_end": 258,
              "support": "Equation (logsq) defines the transition amplitude as c_crit s^{-2} log^2(Omega/omega)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "crit_s_power",
          "value": -2,
          "uncertainty": "source_unspecified",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "power of s in the dipole matrix element and conductivity",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 257,
              "line_end": 258,
              "support": "Equation (logsq) has s^{-2} factor."
            },
            {
              "line_start": 265,
              "line_end": 266,
              "support": "Equation (sigcrit) has s^{-2} factor."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 255,
          "line_end": 258,
          "support": "Stretched-exponential decay psi_0 ~ e^{-s sqrt{x}} and postulated transition amplitude with c_crit s^{-2} log^2(Omega/omega)."
